{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033272-custom-legacy-2e-scales-of-themis-help-needed","id":1033272,"title":"[Custom Legacy, 2E] Scales of Themis - help needed.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-17T05:17:30-08:00","id":1033272,"title":"[Custom Legacy, 2E] Scales of Themis - help needed.","content":"I'm working on a custom legacy for my Acanthus Th\u00e9arch, and wanted to build one that centered around truth and justice and working with the Lex Magica in a more direct way than any of the ones I could find.<br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> It is now presented in what is probably gonna be its final form.<br /> Many thanks to those who helped. Especially <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar346_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"346\" data-vbnamecard=\"346\">Troy</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Scales of Themis.</span></b><br /> Themis was a pre-Hellenistic deity said to be the embodiment of order, law and justice. She represented the divine order of things, in a manner that was far larger than any Man could have thought of. In ancient Sleeper society, her will was often ascribed to that which was undeniably right.<br /> The Greeks developed the concept further, and eventually, <i>themis</i> became a word that meant, \u201cTo put things in their right place\u201d. She became known as the organizer of assemblies, particularly those that dealt with the communal order of things. Her symbol was a perfectly balanced set of scales. This has later spread across the Western hemisphere, as the ideal icon of justice.<br /> It was natural for the Silver Ladder to accept this ideal as their representation of the Lex Magica, and while the order at large strived to enforce this, some mages saw the need to \u201cbalance the scales\u201d as they were. The strove to perfect the laws of Awakened society and make sure that the laws that ruled the Supernal realms carried as much weight in the Fallen world.<br /> The legacy was developed by a cabal of mages, who saw how easily law turned to tyranny and how the will of the Exarchs and the Silver Ladder grew dangerously similar.<br /> They felt the need to correct these laws, to put them out of reach of corruption and personal ambition. They saw in the tales of Themis, how law should neither serve Man nor punish them, but instead provide a frame for man, Awakened and Sleeper to exist.<br /> The Blind are not a police force. They do not spend their time infiltrating law-breakers or investigating crime scenes. This, they leave to the Guardians of the Veil. The Scales of Themis are strong believers in the organization of the Diamond, and are satisfied to make the Lex Magica support this, and leave the different orders and legacies to their own devices \u2013 if in concordance with the Law, of course.<br /> The Scales of Themis work to influence the local Consilia and Convocations in their treatment and development of the Lex Magica, and usually develop considerable political acumen and power. The number of Judges to have fallen to either personal ambition or Tyranny are not few, and the legacy often keeps a good rapport with the Guardians to work against this.<br /> An experienced Themistop\u00f3loi is an asset for a Consilium, as their knowledge of the law is usually unparalleled in a given area. Most Awakened respect this knowledge, and, as the Judge always passes judgment with the letter of the law in hand, their rulings are generally accepted by those involved.<br /> The Judges usually do not care much for the Free Council, as they see their ideals of democracy as almost antithetical to true law and the rightful order of things. If the law can change according to the whims of those it governs, it is not truly a law.<br /> <br /> <b>Origins</b><br /> <b>Parentage:</b> Acanthus or the Silver Ladder.<br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Judges, the Blind, Themistop\u00f3loi.<br /> <b>Background:</b> Many Judges come from a background of Law. Some were police officers, others lawyers, and some even judges. The Judges often have a background in academia and some were engaged in politics, even before Awakening. Common for nearly all of them, however, is an experience with injustice, and a desire to set it right.<br /> <b>Appearance:</b> The Scales of Themis usually present themselves in muted colors and unassuming clothing, the better to subsume the Man when presenting the Law. This also means that keeping up a proper appearance is important, as the Judge represents the Law, and cannot provide others with any means of discrediting them.<br /> As the Mage progresses in the legacy, the spirit of law works its way into his Pattern. A Judge of high Gnosis often has a stern look, and as his understanding of the Law grows, his understanding of humans grows dimmer.<br /> <br /> <b>Doctrine</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 2, Prime 2, Academics 2 with a specialty in Law.<br /> <b>Initiation:</b> A prospective Themistop\u00f3loi must demonstrate a thorough understanding of the local Lex Magica and how it interacts with Sleeper laws and the customs of mage society. Sometimes, this takes the form of an extended debate or lecture, other times, the prospective judge is called upon to serve in a trial, as counsel, judge or jury member.<br /> <b>Organization:</b> The Scales of Themis operate mostly at the command of the local Silver Ladder and the Consilium. Their loyalty should never be divided, as they focus themselves on the Law. Sometimes, this entails being sent to a different Consilium\u2019s territory, if the need for judgment is great enough there.<br /> <b>Theory:</b> There is only Law. The Supernal Truth should govern Awakened society as it did before the Fall. A true law protects and guides those it governs, whereas the laws of Man protects the interests of those who write them.<br /> <br /> <b>Magic</b><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b> Prime<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Succeeding on an Academics roll related to the spell (+2), verbally explaining how a specific law pertains to the situation at hand to an associate (+1) or the target of the spell (+2), researching the laws concerning the target of the spell (+1 to +3, depending on the amount of time spent).<br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Studying or reciting the Lex Magica, debating the law or a specific case with a peer, standing in judgment of a law-breaker.<br /> <br /> <b>Attainments</b><br /> <i>First: Know Transgression</i><br /> <b><i>Prerequisites:</i></b><i> Inititation</i><br /> Themis knows when the natural Law is broken. When the Themistop\u00f3los activates his attainment, he has a small omen of the next violation of the Lex Magica in the area ruled by his Consilium and the path he will need to take to get closer to uncovering it. This only applies to the area under direct and continued sovereignty of the Consilium.<br /> This imitates the Serendipity rote (p. 135) in that it leads the Judge closer to his goal, but has the added restriction that it only applies to violations of the Lex Magica.<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Prime 1<br /> A Judge who possesses at least one dot of Prime, will automatically see through any attempts to hide transgressions against the Lex Magica or the rulings of the Consilium, as per the rote Pierce Deception (p 165). If hidden through magic, this provokes a Clash of Wills.<br /> <i>Second: Keep the Word</i><br /> <b><i>Prerequisites</i></b><i>: Fate 2, the Judge must increase either Empathy, Investigation or Politics to 2 dots </i><br /> A Judge keeps his word and stands by it. This is known by his peers. However, the Judge knows all too well that this trust will not always be rewarded.<br /> The Judge learns to keep an eye on those who swear oaths to him.<br /> Whenever the subject of this spell breaks the Lex Magica or an agreement specifically made between her and the Judge pertaining to this, for example an agreed upon castigation or an oath to uphold it, the Judge receives instant notice of this, briefly has a vision of the transgression and can track the violator until the duration lapses. This emulates <i>Oaths Fulfilled</i>, p135. (Reach spent: +1 Advanced duration, +1 vision, +1 tracking, bonus reach gained from limitations)<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Prime 2<br /> The Judge is known to speak the truth. Those judges who are gifted in the Arcana of Prime can back this up with their magic. If a Judge possesses 2 dots of Prime, those listening to him can hear him and understand him clearly, regardless of distance, noise, or language barriers. Moreover, all subjects know, on a soul-deep level, that what the mage says is true. This only holds up, if the Judge speaks words he knows to be true. (This emulates <i>Words of Truth</i> p.168). This affects those witnessing the activation of the attainment, in which the Judge must recite the oath to be surveilled.<br /> <i>Third: Swear the Oath</i><br /> <b><i>Prerequisites: </i></b><i>Fate 3, Academics 3, the Judge must also increase the skill used to gain the previous</i> <i>attainment to 3 dots, or increase one of the other possible skills to 2 dots.</i><br /> An oath sworn to a Themistop\u00f3los is not a just a collection of words. It carries in it the Supernal order of things and must be in concordance with the Lex Magica. Swearing and confirming the oath takes a scene.<br /> This attainment emulates <i>Sworn Oaths</i>, p.137, but may only be used to craft an oath to uphold or enforce the Lex Magica. This attainment has Advanced Duration.<br /> <b>Optional</b> Prime 3<br /> A Themistop\u00f3los who possesses at least 3 dots of Prime, may grant the subject an additional protection from magical attempts to stop her from fulfilling her vow.<br /> The magic inherent in the vow surrounds the subject and makes her able to Withstand hostile magic with the Potency of the Attainment. This attainment has Advanced Duration.<br /> <i>Fourth: Grant Forgiveness</i><br /> <b><i>Prerequisites: </i></b><i>Fate 4, Academics 4.</i><br /> The Law defines what is right and what is wrong. It describes how to punish those that go against it. But it also tells its subjects what to do with those who have served their time.<br /> The role of the Judge is to investigate, to know and to understand, but it also is to forgive. The Judge may decide the subject has served his time, or that the punishments levied against a subject by others has been unjust and so, may relieve their duress.<br /> The Judge consults the Lex Magica and the rulings made and describes how the subject may overcome their afflictions. The subject\u2019s task depends on the crime or the power of the spell in question. This Attainment functions like Atonement, p138. This Attainment has Advanced Duration.<br /> <b>Optional: </b>Prime 4<br /> The Judge skilled in Prime may wash away the tell-tale signs of sins from their very Pattern. The Judge may remove the marks upon the subject\u2019s soul if she successfully atones for the crime.<br /> This mimics Cleanse Aura, p. 168, but works to remove marks on the soul as well as the signs of Awakened interference. It only works for the marks of the crimes she atones for.<br /> <i>Fifth: Pass Judgment</i><br /> <b><i>Prerequisites: </i></b><i>Fate 5, Academics 5, the Judge must also increase the skill used to gain the second attainment to 4 dots, or increase one of the other possible skills to 3 dots.</i><br /> There is no law if there is no punishment. If upholding the law is the same as breaking it, the law has no consequence but is purely philosophy.<br /> The Themistop\u00f3los makes sure it is not.<br /> The hardest part of a Judge\u2019s work, is understanding a person\u2019s crimes, holding them against the Law, and declaring them guilty. Nonetheless it is also the most important part.<br /> The Judge can levy the power of Pariah, p140, against a breaker of the Lex Magica. The subject must be proven guilty under the Law, and may be given the chance to defend themselves. Refusal to do so means a forfeiture of the right.<br /> This attainment has Advanced Duration.<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Prime 5<br /> The punishment of these supreme Judges is terrible indeed. The world should know of the transgressor\u2019s crimes, and the Judge skilled in Prime, makes sure they do.<br /> When the Judge passes the sentence, they imprint upon the subject a mark that describes them as a breaker of laws and an enemy of the Truth. This is visible to even Peripheral Mage Vision and is instantly understood by all Awakened. Those witnessing the glyph understand the nature of his crimes and instinctively see through all the transgressor\u2019s attempts to conceal or hide the truth. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12700,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","user":"HelloCthulhu","date":". 01-22-2017, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T05:28:31-08:00","id":1033279,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I don't have my pdfs on hand atm, but I'll add some suggestions once I do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:01:02-08:00","id":1033292,"title":"","content":"What do you mean by subtle clue or tic in the Fate Optional? Basically, right now without mechanics that attainment is essentially meaningless, and depending on what you're thinking it might not even be appropriate to use Fate. Can't say for sure yet.<br /> <br /> You may also want to make a note that Pierce Deception has its 1 free Reach spent for (I assume) Instant Activation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:16:54-08:00","id":1033299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033272-custom-legacy-2e-scales-of-themis-help-needed?p=1033292#post1033292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by subtle clue or tic in the Fate Optional? Basically, right now without mechanics that attainment is essentially meaningless, and depending on what you're thinking it might not even be appropriate to use Fate. Can't say for sure yet.<br /> <br /> You may also want to make a note that Pierce Deception has its 1 free Reach spent for (I assume) Instant Activation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was thinking that the attainment, without the optional arcana needs to be activated as an instant action, whereas, with Fate, the subject would have a slip, a tic, a nervous glance or some other unfortunate occurrence, that would tip off the Judge, and let him activate it reflexively in the middle of the conversation, so he might use it without preparation.<br /> <br /> I agree that Fate might be a bit contrived, but a), it's an Acanthus legacy and b), I'd like for it to be possible to use without casting it ahead of every single conversation. Does that make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:24:28-08:00","id":1033307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelloCthulhu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033272-custom-legacy-2e-scales-of-themis-help-needed?p=1033299#post1033299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was thinking that the attainment, without the optional arcana needs to be activated as an instant action, whereas, with Fate, the subject would have a slip, a tic, a nervous glance or some other unfortunate occurrence, that would tip off the Judge, and let him activate it reflexively in the middle of the conversation, so he might use it without preparation.<br /> <br /> I agree that Fate might be a bit contrived, but a), it's an Acanthus legacy and b), I'd like for it to be possible to use without casting it ahead of every single conversation. Does that make sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you assign the one free reach to Advanced Duration, you can make the attainment a ritual that you perform instead. At the lowest level, it would last a week - Two dots of Prime give 1 extra step of Duration, and Prime 2 provides 1 additional spell factor that you can safely apply to Duration. That makes it last a week at the cost of a scene duration ritual once per week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11862,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","user":"Ifisa","date":".  Mrmdubois pointed out I was incorrect about the ritual time. 01-17-2017, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:47:14-08:00","id":1033322,"title":"","content":"A ritual to activate an attainment takes a scene the length of the ritual is not determined by GRI.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T07:14:23-08:00","id":1033340,"title":"","content":"<b>The Legacy --</b> I think this is an awesome concept for a Legacy. It's surprising that something like this hasn't been done before because this Legacy's purpose is one of the core principles behind the Silver Ladder. They have many Silver Ladder Legacies devoted to the priestly, spiritual guidance aspect of the Ladder, but not as many dealing with the Lex Magica, judgment and courtroom type things. So, in that regard, everything you have written for this Legacy thus far look really good and has me intrigued. I can't wait to see more.<br /> <br /> Might I suggestion reversing the Parent Path and Primary Arcanum...<br /> <br /> <b>The Attainment --</b> I like the Attainment and I'm left wondering how much Prime can offer as you progress in your skill with the Arcanum that will also be applicable to the themes and purpose of this Legacy. Prime is good for seeing past deceptions and even illusions and stuff, but once you get to a certain point, Prime no longer applies to those things in a way that would be beneficial. Fate on the other hand is much more in line with the &quot;Scales of Justice&quot; and things like that.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path --</b> If the Parent Path were Obrimos, with their themes of faith, judgment, justice, and conflict, it would make a lot more sense to my mind. These are Silver Ladder Obrimoi who have learned Fate to help them balance the scales against all the falsehoods they can see with their innate magics. Their Awakenings gave them a glimpse at True Law (which is a very Obrimoi type of thing -- very religious sort of experience along the lines of Moses or Mohammed). They gravitate toward this legacy where they can put their keen sense of justice to use by engaging in legal conflicts and things like that ... defending the innocent, prosecuting the guilty, mediating understanding between parties using their knowledge of True Law (Destiny?).<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:21:47-08:00","id":1033485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033272-custom-legacy-2e-scales-of-themis-help-needed?p=1033340#post1033340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Legacy --</b> I think this is an awesome concept for a Legacy. It's surprising that something like this hasn't been done before because this Legacy's purpose is one of the core principles behind the Silver Ladder. They have many Silver Ladder Legacies devoted to the priestly, spiritual guidance aspect of the Ladder, but not as many dealing with the Lex Magica, judgment and courtroom type things. So, in that regard, everything you have written for this Legacy thus far look really good and has me intrigued. I can't wait to see more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I was puzzled by this as well.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <b>The Attainment --</b> I like the Attainment and I'm left wondering how much Prime can offer as you progress in your skill with the Arcanum that will also be applicable to the themes and purpose of this Legacy. Prime is good for seeing past deceptions and even illusions and stuff, but once you get to a certain point, Prime no longer applies to those things in a way that would be beneficial. Fate on the other hand is much more in line with the &amp;quot;Scales of Justice&amp;quot; and things like that. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't actually know the 2e magic system too well, so I wasn't quite sure what the Arcana could bring to the table. I saw that specific Prime rote, and I thought it was a great match. But I haven't actually studied the Arcana thoroughly.<br /> I like Fate to begin with, but I don't know if I could duplicate that effect, as it is spot on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Parent Path --</b> If the Parent Path were Obrimos, with their themes of faith, judgment, justice, and conflict, it would make a lot more sense to my mind. These are Silver Ladder Obrimoi who have learned Fate to help them balance the scales against all the falsehoods they can see with their innate magics. Their Awakenings gave them a glimpse at True Law (which is a very Obrimoi type of thing -- very religious sort of experience along the lines of Moses or Mohammed). They gravitate toward this legacy where they can put their keen sense of justice to use by engaging in legal conflicts and things like that ... defending the innocent, prosecuting the guilty, mediating understanding between parties using their knowledge of True Law (Destiny?).<br /> <br /> What do you think? </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Might I suggestion reversing the Parent Path and Primary Arcanum.. </div> </div> </div>You are completely right. I wrote them to be Obrimos first, but greed, and the fact that my character is sadly an Acanthus made change it. But you are right. It should be an Obrimos legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:31:41-08:00","id":1033494,"title":"","content":"An Acanthus can still join an Obrimos legacy, they just lose out on having a third ruling Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:56:42-08:00","id":1033515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033272-custom-legacy-2e-scales-of-themis-help-needed?p=1033494#post1033494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Acanthus can still join an Obrimos legacy, they just lose out on having a third ruling Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know. Greed, as I said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T08:04:16-08:00","id":1034018,"title":"","content":"I suggest taking a look at the Sisterhood of the Blessed and the Daoine for inspiration on the Attainments. The Sisterhood's focus is personal, the Daoine's focus is retribution ... the Scales of Themis' focus would be on others and on restorative justice. So, having the Prime abilities to see through lies and illusions is a really good tool to have. Fate gives you the ability to find broken promises and know when something is true even if the person speaking doesn't know it's true. Then you also have the power to then <i>know</i> how things are <i>supposed to be</i>; that is a great tool as well. I can see those abilities being the lower Attainments. Then Fate gives you the power to &quot;put things right&quot; with as much or as little subtlety as you want with all kinds of conditional hexes and curses and blessings and things. Also, don't forget to tie the Attainments power into the Lex Magica. A Silver Ladder Legacy would have it no other way. Perhaps your Attainments work especially well when your dealing with upholding the Lex or something.<br /> <br /> I was also going to suggest something for the Doctrine... Rather than Academics (or in addition to it), perhaps Politics would be a good choice? Politics represents the ability to get things done using the right rules, the right people, the right ins and outs of a system.<br /> <br /> I think it's a great idea... using the <b>True Law</b> as a metaphor or stand-in for other concepts like karma and destiny and things like that. &quot;That's not just a run of bad luck you're having. It's restitution. You're paying your penance. You have transgressed against the Law. I will bring you justice.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T10:59:06-08:00","id":1034118,"title":"","content":"How about making a a secondary prerequisite, that is 1 dot in either Politics, Investigation or Empathy? These could go up with the attainment progression.<br /> <br /> Regarding tying the Attainments into the Lex Magica, I was considering making the first one constant, but only spot when the target was lying about transgressions against the law. However, I don't really see a way to do that through the Fate Arcanum.<br /> The problem is, that Fate, as I see it, mostly deals with punishment, whereas I'm looking more into interrogation and/or spotting the lie or the transgressions.<br /> <br /> Howabout adding Fate or \u00bdGnosis dots to rolls made to deal with law?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T14:06:57-08:00","id":1034231,"title":"","content":"Oaths Fulfilled would make a good later attainment for determining transgressions against the Lex. Basically you would just state that you're investigating an individual for a set period of time (Though since attainments don't take up spell control you could have multiple &quot;investigations&quot; running simultaneously) and use the attainment, if they're committing the type of crime you suspect (Breaking the Lex) then Fate informs you.<br /> <br /> Also, Fate is good for finding transgressors, for instance Serendipity without Reach would send you a clear omen to lead you to your next criminal investigation.<br /> <br /> Prime would serve as your backup arcana to cut through any lies or Veils and protect you from criminal magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T01:13:39-08:00","id":1034483,"title":"","content":"That's a really good suggestion! Maybe a modified Oaths Fulfilled for the first attainment. Something like you instantly know when a person breaks the agreement to speak the truth in an interrogation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T03:32:32-08:00","id":1034508,"title":"","content":"You could do that, but I wouldn't. I'd use Serendipity as the first attainment. It's initial ability is really useful and can basically serve as a plot hook generator for the ST and the ability needs to only spend its 1 Reach on being Instant. <br /> <br /> Oaths Fulfilled becomes most cool when employing its Reach effects. You could have it anywhere between the 2nd and 4th Attainment. If you restricted it's use to alerting you to when a subject breaks the Lex I'd throw in a free Reach so you can get more out of it as a lower level attainment. For instance you could have it as the 3rd attainment that way, have all the Reach clauses active and activate it as an Instant action.<br /> <br /> Since Mages usually pick up the first and second attainment simultaneously you also wouldn't be making a Mage hold off on getting that cool power if you made it a second attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T05:15:12-08:00","id":1034528,"title":"","content":"Great suggestions. Any ideas on how to incorporate Prime?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T06:01:58-08:00","id":1034542,"title":"","content":"Well, Pierce Deception is obviously going to be your first Optional attainment. I'll think on the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T06:17:44-08:00","id":1034548,"title":"","content":"Sworn Oaths and Display of Power could probably work as the third/fourth Attainments for Fate and Prime respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T06:29:23-08:00","id":1034553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033272-custom-legacy-2e-scales-of-themis-help-needed?p=1034548#post1034548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sworn Oaths and Display of Power could probably work as the third/fourth Attainments for Fate and Prime respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sworn Oaths I agree, but what's the rationale for Display of Power? It doesn't seem like it would be useful unless you have the +2 Reach for Rote counterspelling which would make it the 5th attainment if you want it to be Instant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T06:44:09-08:00","id":1034561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033272-custom-legacy-2e-scales-of-themis-help-needed?p=1034553#post1034553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sworn Oaths I agree, but what's the rationale for Display of Power? It doesn't seem like it would be useful unless you have the +2 Reach for Rote counterspelling which would make it the 5th attainment if you want it to be Instant.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about either Wards and Signs or Words of Truth?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T06:50:26-08:00","id":1034563,"title":"","content":"Words of Truth would be really good for delivering testimony or receiving a confession. Wards andSigns isn't bad, but it's also pretty situational.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T07:06:43-08:00","id":1034574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033272-custom-legacy-2e-scales-of-themis-help-needed?p=1034563#post1034563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Words of Truth would be really good for delivering testimony or receiving a confession. Wards andSigns isn't bad, but it's also pretty situational.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it'd be Sworn Oaths and Words of Truth at the third Attainment for the Scales?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T07:17:54-08:00","id":1034578,"title":"","content":"I wrote a similar Legacy for one of my players, once. Only got as far as the first 3 attainments, which I'll put up as soon as I get off work.<br /> One of the attainments was something like &quot;When you roll a CoW to find something supernaturally hidden (Veiling spell, Obfuscate, and so on), you can spend 1 Mana for automatic successes equal to Fate dots&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T07:18:12-08:00","id":1034579,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think that works best. *Rereads Words of Truth* Huh, I had never realized before that the subject of the spell isn't the Mage. You could cast that spell and say something true and only the subject of the spell would have to believe you not just anyone listening. I'm not sure but this might also mean you can't use it as a tool for confession, just testimony. I think I'd spend the Reach for Advanced Scale so not only can you be heard easily in a large area but everyone in it believes your words. This also explains the distance thing, cast the spell and for the Duration the subject can hear you wherever he goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-19-2017, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T11:14:16-08:00","id":1034731,"title":"","content":"How about this for a first attainment:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>First: Know Transgression</b><br /> Themis knows when the natural Law is broken. The Judge receives an instant premonition of the next violation of the Lex Magica in the area ruled by his Consilium and the path he will need to take to get closer to uncovering it. This requires the Judge to engage in a ritual casting weekly, but will then last for the next seven days.<br /> This imitates the Serendipity rote (p. 135) in that it leads the Judge closer to his goal, but has the added restriction that it only applies to violations of the Lex Magica.<br /> Optional: Prime 1<br /> A Judge who possesses at least one dot of Prime, will automatically see through any attempts to hide transgressions against the Lex Magica or the rulings of the Consilium, as per the rote Pierce Deception (p 165). If hidden through magic, this provokes a Clash of Wills.<br /> First: Know Transgression<br /> Themis knows when the natural Law is broken. The Judge receives an instant premonition of the next violation of the Lex Magica in the area ruled by his Consilium and the path he will need to take to get closer to uncovering it. This requires the Judge to engage in a ritual casting weekly, but will then last for the next seven days.<br /> This imitates the Serendipity rote (p. 135) in that it leads the Judge closer to his goal, but has the added restriction that it only applies to violations of the Lex Magica.<br /> <i>Optional: Prime 1</i><br /> A Judge who possesses at least one dot of Prime, will automatically see through any attempts to hide transgressions against the Lex Magica or the rulings of the Consilium, as per the rote Pierce Deception (p 165). If hidden through magic, this provokes a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <br /> My thought was, that downgrading it to ritual casting and severely limiting its scope was enough to give me the 2 Reach needed for an advanced duration of one week, making it all-round useful for both the mage and the ST, and also giving that feeling of inevitability of the law.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T11:39:38-08:00","id":1034748,"title":"","content":"You could get Advanced Duration for one Reach, but I'm not sure it's supposed to ping the Mage with an omen like that. Duration doesn't actually seem to do anything for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-19-2017, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T12:23:51-08:00","id":1034776,"title":"","content":"1 Reach only gives a duration of one day.<br /> <br /> Is it too powerful or too general?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T12:50:25-08:00","id":1034790,"title":"","content":"You're reading how Reach works for Advanced Spell Factoes incorrectly. Regardless Serendipity with Advanced Duration isn't too powerful, it's just that Duration doesn't help it do anything at all. That's why it's Potency Primary in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:05:25-08:00","id":1034806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033272-custom-legacy-2e-scales-of-themis-help-needed?p=1034748#post1034748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could get Advanced Duration for one Reach, but I'm not sure it's supposed to ping the Mage with an omen like that. Duration doesn't actually seem to do anything for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>For effects like that, they're supposed to reoccur once per Ritual Casting Interval, no?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a spell would logically have an immediate effect but is cast with Advanced<br /> Duration, the effect recurs at every multiple of the character\u2019s Gnosis-<br /> based ritual casting time, until the Duration runs out. For example,<br /> a Gnosis 1 character\u2019s healing spell with a Duration of a day heals<br /> its Potency in Health boxes every three hours. </div> </div> </div>In this case, they'd get one Omen per Interval.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:09:23-08:00","id":1034809,"title":"","content":"Yes, but that's not as good as being able to do it at will which is what you'd get if you just spent the Reach on Instant Activation. Hence, Advanced Duration doesn't do anything for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T21:43:25-08:00","id":1035059,"title":"","content":"Oh, okay. I understand now. The Magic system is hard.<br /> <br /> The thing that I wanted to do, however, is change it from the insta-omen of Serendipity to a longer lasting effect that represented getting in tune with the Lex.<br /> Otherwise, I sorta feel like he'd have to go around activating the Legacy all the time, and it'd feel a bit more contrived.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12700,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","user":"HelloCthulhu","date":". 01-20-2017, 04:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T00:50:09-08:00","id":1035117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033272-custom-legacy-2e-scales-of-themis-help-needed?p=1034806#post1034806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For effects like that, they're supposed to reoccur once per Ritual Casting Interval, no?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In this case, they'd get one Omen per Interval.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The problem with this is, that the Mage would have no reason to cast it that often, unless they knew that a crime would occur.<br /> Although, keeping it as-is would make it into more of an investigation theme, which could work. The optional would then be tied to the transgressor? How long would that effect last?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not quite sure what the rules are for creating attainments. Do all the primary effects have to be from the Ruling Arcana?<br /> <br /> I'd like to have Words of Truth as the second attainment, but that's obviously Prime. Would I need to find a way to make it Fate, or could I keep it as it is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12700,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","user":"HelloCthulhu","date":". 01-20-2017, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T02:03:48-08:00","id":1035133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelloCthulhu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033272-custom-legacy-2e-scales-of-themis-help-needed?p=1035059#post1035059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that I wanted to do, however, is change it from the insta-omen of Serendipity to a longer lasting effect that represented getting in tune with the Lex.<br /> Otherwise, I sorta feel like he'd have to go around activating the Legacy all the time, and it'd feel a bit more contrived.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you are attuned to the Lex, as it is now you find information about or relating to in some way information about the Lex everywhere you look. Think about the activation of the ability as one of those &quot;Aha!&quot; moments of insight people sometimes get when reflecting on religious texts. Except that a member of this legacy has those almost all the time and at will from constantly thinking about the Lex. Now, what the attainment doesn't do right now is prevent you from using it to gain an omen about any course of action you want to take, it's not restricted to the Lex. Maybe it was designed that way to make life a little easier for members of the legacy. On the other hand if you add the restriction to the Lex you can give it some more oomph, but I don't have any good ideas for that.<br /> <br /> Primary attainments should all be from the same arcana, Optional Attainments should all be from the same arcana. Fortunately, Prime is your Optional Arcana so Words of Truth can be an attainment, just not the Primary one. As I noted before Words of Truth is a spell you cast on someone else so that they can hear and understand you and be convinced of the truth you're speaking. To that end if you make it Optional attainment #2 and spend the Reach on Instant Activation then it will work on targets you're touching (Up to 2) or on targets in an area centered on the Mage (Up to a Large room at Prime 5). The effect will last at best 3 turns (Usually enough time to testify , but if not they can just keep reactivating). Also because the spell is Withstood it won't be useful in an offensive manner (Forcing people to believe you) until you hit Prime 3 and above. It will never work on some people or ephemeral entities. Fortunately, most of the people you'd use it on probably want to hear what you have to say anyway. If you restricted it to allowing you to only talk about the Lex or on Lex related matters you could get another Reach to spend, perhaps on Advanced Duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T02:17:35-08:00","id":1035137,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think you are right. I'll follow your advice.<br /> <br /> Regarding optional attainments, I was under the impression that they modified the primary? Can they provide completely separate effects?<br /> <br /> Sorry for all the questions. I really appreciate you taking your time to help me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T02:43:55-08:00","id":1035141,"title":"","content":"Optional Attainments can provide separate effects, its important that attainments synergize with each other in order to work for the overall legacy, but they don't need to be limited to modifying Primary attainments to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T09:10:17-08:00","id":1035261,"title":"","content":"I like it. It makes sense.<br /> <br /> I would keep in mind that Attainments can kind of stretch the boundaries a bit of the normal rules. I know you want to avoid something being overpowered, but I think that something like that is a problem on paper rather than in actual play. If the Attainment works for your theme and sticks to your theme, then it's hard for it to be overpowered. In many cases you'll find us saying that something sound very underpowered once you get to your third or fourth attainment because that instinct to downplay things is still kicking in when you're writing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:04:02-08:00","id":1035318,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\">Thanks to all your great suggestions, I have come up with five Attainments. I'm still missing the optional for the fourth one, so I'd love suggestions for that.<br /> I'd also like to hear what you think about these.<br /> <br /> <b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Attainments </div> </div> </div></b></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>First: Know Transgression</i></span><br /> <b><i>Prerequisites:</i></b><i> Inititation</i><br /> Themis knows when the natural Law is broken. When the Themistop\u00f3los of the next violation of the Lex Magica in the area ruled by his Consilium and the path he will need to take to get closer to uncovering it.<br /> This imitates the Serendipity rote (p. 135) in that it leads the Judge closer to his goal, but has the added restriction that it only applies to violations of the Lex Magica.<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Prime 1<br /> A Judge who possesses at least one dot of Prime, will automatically see through any attempts to hide transgressions against the Lex Magica or the rulings of the Consilium, as per the rote Pierce Deception (p 165). If hidden through magic, this provokes a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Second: Keep the Word</i></span><br /> <b><i>Prerequisites</i></b><i>: Fate 2, the Judge must increase either Empathy, Investigation or Politics to 2 dots </i><br /> A Judge keeps his word and stands by it. This is known by his peers. However, the Judge knows all too well that this trust will not always be rewarded.<br /> The Judge learns to keep an eye on those who swear oaths to him.<br /> Whenever the subject of this spell breaks the Lex Magica or an agreement specifically made between her and the Judge pertaining to this, for example an agreed upon castigation or an oath to uphold it, the Judge receives instant notice of this, briefly has a vision of the transgression and can track the violator until a day has passed. This emulates <i>Oaths Fulfilled</i>, p135. (Reach spent: +1 Advanced duration, +1 vision, +1 tracking, bonus reach gained from limitations)<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Prime 2<br /> The Judge is known to speak the truth. Those judges who are gifted in the Arcana of Prime can back this up with their magic. If a Judge possesses 2 dots of Prime, those listening to him can hear him and understand him clearly, regardless of distance, noise, or language barriers. Moreover, all subjects know, on a soul-deep level, that what the mage says is true. This only holds up, if the Judge speaks words he knows to be true. (This emulates <i>Words of Truth</i> p.168)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Third: Swear the Oath</i></span><br /> <b><i>Prerequisites: </i></b><i>Fate 3, Academics 3, the Judge must also increase the skill used to gain the previous</i> <i>attainment to 3 dots, or increase one of the other possible skills to 2 dots.</i><br /> An oath sworn to a Themistop\u00f3los is not a just a collection of words. It carries in it the Supernal order of things and must be in concordance with the Lex Magica.<br /> This attainment emulates <i>Sworn Oaths</i>, p.137, but may only be used to craft an oath to uphold or enforce the Lex Magica. This attainment has Advanced Duration.<br /> <b>Optional</b> Prime 3<br /> A Themistop\u00f3los who possesses at least 3 dots of Prime, may grant the subject an additional protection from magical attempts to stop her from fulfilling her vow.<br /> The magic inherent in the vow surrounds the subject and makes her able to Withstand hostile magic with the Potency of the Attainment.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Fourth: Grant Forgiveness</i></span><br /> <b><i>Prerequisites: </i></b><i>Fate 4, Academics 4.</i><br /> The Law defines what is right and what is wrong. It describes how to punish those that go against it. But it also tells its subjects what to do with those who have served their time.<br /> The role of the Judge is to investigate, to know and to understand, but it also is to forgive. The Judge may decide the subject has served his time, or that the punishments levied against a subject by others has been unjust and so, may relieve their duress.<br /> The Judge consults the Lex Magica and the rulings made and describes how the subject may overcome their afflictions. The subject\u2019s task depends on the crime or the power of the spell in question. This Attainment functions like Atonement, p138.<br /> <b>Optional: </b>Prime<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Fifth: Pass Judgment</i></span><br /> <b><i>Prerequisites: </i></b><i>Fate 5, Academics 5, the Judge must also increase the skill used to gain the second attainment to 4 dots, or increase one of the other possible skills to 3 dots.</i><br /> There is no law if there is no punishment. If upholding the law is the same as breaking it, the law has no consequence but is purely philosophy.<br /> The Themistop\u00f3los makes sure it is not.<br /> The hardest part of a Judge\u2019s work, is understanding a person\u2019s crimes, holding them against the Law, and declaring them guilty. Nonetheless it is also the most important part.<br /> The Judge can levy the power of Pariah, p140, against a breaker of the Lex Magica. The subject must be proven guilty under the Law, and may be given the chance to defend themselves. Refusal to do so, means a forfeiture of the right.<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Prime 4<br /> The punishment of these supreme Judges is terrible indeed. The world should know of the transgressor\u2019s crimes, and the Judge skilled in Prime, makes sure they do.<br /> When the Judge passes the sentence, they imprint upon the subject a mark that describes them as a breaker of laws and an enemy of the Truth. This is visible to even Peripheral Mage Vision and is instantly understood by all Awakened. Their reaction is not guaranteed, however. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:08:23-08:00","id":1035441,"title":"","content":"1st attainment should have a means of establishing the area he can monitor. Perhaps since he's restricted to detecting omens of violations of the Lex he could perform a walking/patrol ritual over an area of Advanced Scale.<br /> <br /> 2nd attainment's Duration is wrong, with Advanced Duration it will last a day when they first get their attainment but by Fate 5 it will last a -year-.<br /> Prime Optional: Only subjects of his attainment who hear him will believe he's speaking the truth on a soul deep level. You need to establish the mechanics by which you determine the subjects of the attainment. As it stands now he would need to touch the subject to convey the truth and would only be able to convince two people at a time or a small room at Prime 5.<br /> <br /> Third attainment is fine, I assume the magical protection is a combined effect with the swearing of the Oath so it should also receive Advanced Duration and you have another Reach to spend on it if you want (Though I'm not sure for what so leaving it as is would be fine). Should note that validating the Oath takes a scene.<br /> <br /> Fourth attainment needs Advanced Duration to grant enough time to complete Atonement, this should give them about a week I believe. I haven't got a good idea for the Optional, sorry.<br /> <br /> Fifth Attainment: Use Advanced Duration again, since its limited in scope I would go ahead and say that the Judge has the option to levy Pariah against a target for a year and a day. Takes a ritual to activate.<br /> Prime Optional is incorrectly labeled as Prime 4, cool idea though. I'd give it some mechanical oomph beyond being a magical warning label, not sure what though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T02:02:50-08:00","id":1035661,"title":"","content":"Good stuff. I'll mull it over.<br /> <br /> One thing, and I'm sorry to sound dense. On which page is the description of how Advanced Duration increases with Arcana(/successes?)?<br /> I thought moving more steps in Advanced Duration required penalties to the roll?<br /> How will the Second attainment last a year, for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T05:41:42-08:00","id":1035686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelloCthulhu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033272-custom-legacy-2e-scales-of-themis-help-needed?p=1035661#post1035661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good stuff. I'll mull it over.<br /> <br /> One thing, and I'm sorry to sound dense. On which page is the description of how Advanced Duration increases with Arcana(/successes?)?<br /> I thought moving more steps in Advanced Duration required penalties to the roll?<br /> How will the Second attainment last a year, for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Advanced Duration chart is on page 113. If it's the primary factor of the spell, it will start at a level equal to your dots in the Arcana (4 dots = One month), if not, it starts at the first level (scene).<br /> <br /> Successes never impact Spell Factors in any way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T05:41:58-08:00","id":1035687,"title":"","content":"Spells and attainments go up by a number of primary factors equal to your rank in the arcana automatically. This still holds true if you switch to Advanced Factors. You can read about attainments and factors on pg. 198 under Legacy Attainments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T05:52:18-08:00","id":1035689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033272-custom-legacy-2e-scales-of-themis-help-needed?p=1035687#post1035687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spells and attainments go up <b>by</b> a number of primary factors equal to your rank in the arcana automatically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Small correction - they go up by Arcana -1 (or up <b>to</b> your Arcana level, to word it less confusingly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T10:42:12-08:00","id":1035755,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I finally think I get it.<br /> <br /> I updated the original post with the revised Attainments and the optional for the fourth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T10:57:35-08:00","id":1035757,"title":"","content":"The bit about tracking until a day has passed in the 2nd attainment should probably be removed because I think that effect would last until the Duration lapses.<br /> <br /> By the way, the Guardians would also be keenly interested in this legacy due to its super-surveillance and punishment potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T11:07:53-08:00","id":1035762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033272-custom-legacy-2e-scales-of-themis-help-needed?p=1035757#post1035757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bit about tracking until a day has passed in the 2nd attainment should probably be removed because I think that effect would last until the Duration lapses.<br /> <br /> By the way, the Guardians would also be keenly interested in this legacy due to its super-surveillance and punishment potential.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fixed.<br /> <br /> I've got two Guardian Cabal members, and I do so love to watch them beg.<br /> <br /> Nah, in all seriousness, I couldn't see the Silver Ladder being too interested in sharing this with the Guardians. The law has a tendency to twist behind the veils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12700,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","user":"HelloCthulhu","date":". 01-21-2017, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T10:56:07-08:00","id":1036162,"title":"","content":"What about the Prime attainment being something the limits the magical effectiveness of the person being judge or punished or whatever. Like, they have a Threshold they have to overcome before they're spells even fire off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:09:02-08:00","id":1036172,"title":"","content":"Prime can do that? Are you talking about the fifth Optional? I made a clause about being unable to lie about your crimes in it. But sure, it coulf carry a bit more oomph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:12:46-08:00","id":1036175,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I think the way I would run it is that it places an automatic Withstand on your ability to place spells, so to get a spell off requires that you pump Potency.<br /> <br /> Personally though, I like the Prime 5 attainment as is, it's clean mechanically and fits thematically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}